## Interface: 30300
## Title: Felsworn
## Notes: Felfury and Inner Demon tracking for the Felsworn class, plus defensive class-UI constants so party and raid frames survive a Felsworn in the group.
## Author: wowserver
## Version: 1.0
## SavedVariables: FelswornSaved
## DefaultState: enabled

# Load order matters.
#   Core.lua declares the Felsworn table, Say(), the saved-variable defaults and the event
#   frame, so it has to come first -- everything below stores itself into that table.
#   ClassUI.lua runs its whole job at load time and is deliberately NOT class-gated: the
#   character who crashes on a missing CLASS_ICON_TCOORDS.FELSWORN is the priest standing
#   next to the Felsworn, not the Felsworn. See the header of that file.
#   Felfury.lua is class-gated and does nothing until Core calls it at PLAYER_LOGIN.
#
# There is no Bindings.xml. The Demon Hunter that previously occupied this class slot bound two
# keys for double jump and glide; Felsworn has no movement abilities at all, so the file was
# removed rather than left empty -- an empty Bindings.xml still creates a header in the Key
# Bindings panel with nothing under it.
Core.lua
ClassUI.lua
Felfury.lua
